=== REASONING ===
Why the selected design preserves ADR-015, P1-P10, and the non-AI baseline.

1. Baseline coexistence (P10): The deterministic heuristic at
   GET /api/v1/vehicles/{vehicleID}/range/projection is untouched.
   The new POST /api/v1/ai/ml/range/train is opt-in per feature
   (DefaultOn=false), and AI Mode = off causes the
   ai.GuardedHandler to 404 the route before any provider is
   constructed (proven by TestRangePredictionModelAIOffUsesHeuristicOnly).

2. Single registry entry (P9): The feature is registered exactly
   once with explicit, populated RouteSet metadata. Empty
   surfaces are explicit `[]string{}` per the Phase-50
   methodology, never omitted.

3. Strategy isolation (P4 + P5): The AI path is a strategy
   package importing only `dispatch`, `provider`, `stream`, and
   the redactadapter wrapper. Provider adapters are NEVER imported
   from feature code (P1). The decorator chain is applied through
   `provider.For(...)` in the handler — redaction → rate limit →
   cost cap → audit → trace, in the locked order.

4. Read-only tools (P5 propose-only contract): Both
   `train_range_model` and `query_range_prediction` are
   `Mutates: false`. The trainer reads from `drives` only; it
   never writes to `drives` and never overwrites the heuristic
   curve. The single mutating surface (the canonical projection
   page) is unchanged.

5. Per-bucket fallback parity (P10 strict): Each of the 12
   (TempBucket × SpeedBucket) entries with fewer than
   mlrange.DefaultMinSamplesPerBucket=5 qualifying drives in the
   lookback window falls back to mlrange.HeuristicWhPerKm at the
   bucket's representative midpoint
   (temp=-5/5/20/30 °C, speed=35/70/110 km/h). The hot midpoint is
   deliberately at 30 (not >35) so the legacy `tempC>35` 1.08
   multiplier in defaultEfficiency does NOT silently fire — the
   midpoint matches the bucket label "hot ≥25 °C" range. Pinned
   in TestHeuristicWhPerKm_PinnedValues + the cross-package
   parity test TestRangeFallbackParity_APIvsMLRange.

6. Provider-egress contract (I4): With ai_mode='off', the
   ai.GuardedHandler short-circuits before NewHandler's inner
   logic runs. The Go off-mode test asserts the
   GUARD_BYPASSED side-channel is NEVER triggered — proving no
   provider is constructed and no LLM byte ever leaves the
   process in off mode.

7. SI canonical (Phase-42): All trainer inputs come from the
   canonical SI columns
   (avg_speed_mps, ambient_temp_c_avg, distance_m, energy_used_wh).
   Conversion to display-friendly Wh/km + km/h happens in Go
   inside the AIDriveStatsSource pgx adapter; the tool payloads
   carry SI-derived units (Wh/km is canonical here per
   `unit-conversion.instructions.md` §"Energy efficiency").
   No ai_mode='off' path adds new SI-suffixed columns or fields.

8. SPA wiring (P11/P12 + W1 inline): AIRangePrediction wires
   end-to-end to POST /ai/ml/range/train via useAiStream — no
   placeholder strings (verified by Select-String over allowed
   files: 0 matches in this slice's component), the primary
   action button's `disabled` is a computed
   `!canGenerate = !(vehicleId != null && stream.state !==
   'streaming')`, double-submit guard is exercised by
   TestRangePredictionModelAIOnWiredCallsRoute test #2.

